            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I have this problem too. My colorscheme sets \n```\nVisual         xxx ctermfg=15 ctermbg=0 guifg=#eeeeee guibg=#0087af\n```\nSince d1dd7c5d45b4ad86631b7954e8a651a0ba547854, the `guifg=#eeeeee` also applies to the cursor:\n<img width=\"590\" height=\"124\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/e2140f63-a9bc-4ff3-90d8-59d0e6ad5012\" />\nBefore the patch, the highlighting would not apply to the cursor, and cursor would instead look as if there was no Visual selection:\n\nwith visual:\n<img width=\"627\" height=\"133\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/9e2f92e8-5048-436c-be50-71b5d3ea836e\" />\n\nwithout visual:\n<img width=\"609\" height=\"118\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/03dcb51b-700c-4a5e-83ef-679124936665\" />\n\nDefining Visual like this:\n```\nVisual         xxx ctermfg=15 ctermbg=0 guibg=#0087af\n```\ni.e. removing guifg=, the cursor again uses the Cursor highlighting, but it makes it worse on the eyes:\n<img width=\"620\" height=\"122\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/1e0febcc-b012-4a80-8dc0-9be7bc07db2b\" />\n\nI am using Kitty.\n\nAs a workaround, I just use the default Visual highlighting, it looks good enough.\n\nThe issue is more prominent for character-wise visual mode:\n<img width=\"519\" height=\"115\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/12e1fa01-b0d9-4280-aca6-22057b56faa1\" />\nThe colon here is selected too, which is not at all obvious.",
