            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Could the issue be resolved by using:\n`:set guicursor+=v:hor20-reverse`\n?\n\nCould Neovim's default for 'guicursor' be updated accordingly?\n\nI've tried that 'guicursor' setting in Windows Terminal, gnome-terminal and kitty and it looks fine to me. How do others feel about it?\n\nIn gnome-terminal 3.52.0 a visual selection in Neovim (both 0.12.5 and 0.13.0-dev-1840) looks like:\n<img width=\"108\" height=\"86\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/86ad9ebc-8298-4fab-8c70-b70cf5449470\" />\n(default settings, but \"v:hor20-reverse\" included in 'guicursor').\n\nOne could revert https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/42105. Some possible reasons to not revert it though:\n- the appearance of the cell with the cursor changes on entering Visual mode giving the user immediate confirmation that Visual mode has been entered.\n- internal changes: 56 less lines of code (the special handling relating to `noinvcur` was removed), and some test cases might make more sense as Visual highlighting always applies to all characters within the visual selection (the character at the cursor position isn't left out).",
