            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": ">  I tried `:set guicursor+=v:hor20-reverse` and it makes things worse for me.\n> ...\n>      With this setup, cursor is not clearly seen whether it's at the of the selection or in the middle (for line visual).\n\nOk, that cursor is really hard to see, especially because it's the same color as the background of the surrounding text. How much of a problem is it really though if the cursor column is hard to see when making a line-wise selection? (The cursor column doesn't affect the lines selected.)\n\n(In the case of a character-wise selection, I assume it'd still be easy to track the cursor position - it will be at one end of the selection.)\n\nI think the image I gave above shows that `v:hor20-reverse` looks ok with the default colorscheme. Maybe `v:hor20-reverse` is still worth considering for the default and the option can be changed as needed when using a different colorscheme?",
