        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "\n> Ok, that cursor is really hard to see, especially because it's the same color as the background of the surrounding text. How much of a problem is it really though if the cursor column is hard to see when making a line-wise selection? (The cursor column doesn't affect the lines selected.)\n\nIt is quite the problem for me, I regularly switch between visual modes. For example, I do a line visual, and then I figure out that I actually needed visual-block/visual-char after that. So I would move the cursor to where I want it to be, and then switch to visual-block. Though like I said, it seems that this issue can be solved by just changing the colorscheme which I'm fine with.\n>(In the case of a character-wise selection, I assume it'd still be easy to track the cursor position - it will be at one end of the selection.)\n\nThis is untrue for me, as the cursor could be at either end of the selection. Also, I regularly enter visual mode, and use, e.g. `e` to increase my selection. I have regularly overshot the selection by one character (as the cursor would invisible). With `:set guicursor=v:hor10-Visual` this could probably be solved (i.e. the overshoot by one problem), however, it still keeps the cursor invisible (or rather, the cursor is the same color as the selection).",
            "created_at": "2026-10-15T08:23:03Z",
